# .mergeignore — paths kept off the published branch.
#
# utils/publish.sh reads this file from the source branch (`dev`) and drops every
# path it matches from the published snapshot. It always drops this file itself,
# so there is no need to list it.
#
# Each non-comment line is a git pathspec. A trailing slash is stripped, and the
# line is prefixed with `:(glob)` unless it already begins with `:`. That means:
#
#   utils        a bare directory matches everything beneath it
#   *.md         matches top-level files only, because `*` does not cross a `/`
#   docs/**      use `**` to recurse
#
# A path that no tracked file matches is a harmless no-op, so entries may be
# listed defensively before the file they name exists.
#
# Never list a bundle directory, `README.md`, or `LICENSE`: publish.sh refuses to
# build a snapshot that omits them, and every bundle is validated after filtering.

# Maintenance tooling: only ever runs on the development branch.
utils

# Development notes and contributor documentation.
CONTRIBUTING.md
TODO.md
